      "title": "Note: Loading Longer Videos",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "In the Load Video node, the 'frame_load_cap' metric (when set to 0) will show the total number of frames in a darker grey. Loading more than 200 frames will likely cause memory issues, so we need to limit the number of frames we render in one run and also use a hefty machine (minimum large and extra large machine).\n\nStart with 64 frames per batch using the batch manager. If you don't use this, you will throttle your memory regardless of machine size.\n\n"
